# Vanilla Web Development

## Stack

- Use **HTML5**, **modern CSS** (Flexbox/Grid), and **ECMAScript ES2024+**
- Use **ES Modules** for all JavaScript — `import`/`export` only; no script-tag globals or ad-hoc IIFEs

## Dependencies

- Prefer **native Web APIs** (Fetch, Crypto, Storage) for trivial tasks — avoid heavy packages for simple problems
- When a library is warranted, favor **established, well-maintained NPM packages** instead of reinventing wheels
- Before adding a dependency, search [npmjs.com](https://www.npmjs.com/) for the most downloaded standard choice:
  - Dates → `date-fns`
  - Validation → `zod`

## User Experience

- When the user must wait for data or any async operation, show a **loading indicator** (spinner, skeleton, or progress state) so they know something is happening
- Use **shimmer placeholders** on images so slow network loads feel smooth instead of jumping in abruptly

## Accessibility & Code Quality

- **Semantic HTML:** use proper elements and landmarks for screen readers and keyboard navigation
- **WCAG color:** meet contrast ratios (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text); never rely on color alone to convey meaning
- **Theming:** CSS custom properties for colors, spacing, and typography
- **Clean code:** early returns, descriptive naming, single-responsibility functions
